{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For yet seven days.</b> These are the seven days of mourning for Methuselah the righteous — the Holy One, blessed be He, had pity on his honor and delayed the punishment. Go and calculate the years of Methuselah and you will find that they end in year 600 of Noah's life (Sanhedrin 108b)." "<b>For yet days.</b> What is עוֹד? A period after this period — added to the 120 years." "<b>Forty days.</b> Corresponding to the formation of the embryo — for they corrupted themselves to trouble their Maker to form the shape of mamzerim."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:51.249976109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}